{
  "name": "670. GitHub Copilot routes and sign-in (copilot routes)",
  "description": "GitHub Copilot routing and Sign in with GitHub. Copilot rejects a bare-string embeddings input with a body-less 400, so a single input must go out as string[] (red before: 670.1 answered 400). Claude models are served from Copilot's Anthropic-compatible /v1/messages, reached from /v1/chat/completions (unary and streamed), /v1/responses and the native /anthropic route; rows read the provider-bound body back from extra_fields.raw_request (send_back_raw_request is on in the profile) and assert the Messages shape (top-level system, no Responses input). OpenAI models that advertise the Responses API go to Copilot's native /responses rather than through Chat Completions (raw body carries input, not messages). /v1/models lists the provider's models per key. The sign-in rows exercise the gateway's device-flow proxy: start returns a real GitHub device code (free, nothing is approved), an unknown device code and a missing one answer 400, and sign-in on any other provider answers 400. Inference rows need GITHUB_COPILOT_API_KEY (a fine-grained PAT with Copilot Requests) and run only under PROVIDER=github-copilot.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "670.1 github-copilot/text-embedding-3-small /v1/embeddings single string input is sent as an array (copilot routes)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "function rawRequest(j) {",
              "  var rr = j && j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.raw_request;",
              "  if (typeof rr === 'string') { try { rr = JSON.parse(rr); } catch (e) { rr = null; } }",
              "  return rr;",
              "}",
              "pm.test('670.1 github-copilot/text-embedding-3-small /v1/embeddings single string input is sent as an array (copilot routes) answers 200', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 500)).to.equal(200);",
              "});",
              "if (pm.response.code !== 200) { return; }",
              "var j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('one embedding comes back', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(j.data, 'data: ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 300)).to.be.an('array').with.lengthOf(1);",
              "  pm.expect(j.data[0].embedding, 'embedding vector').to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Copilot received input as string[] (it 400s on a bare string)', function () {",
              "  var rr = rawRequest(j);",
              "  pm.expect(rr, 'extra_fields.raw_request missing - is send_back_raw_request on for github-copilot?').to.be.an('object');",
              "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(rr.input), 'raw input: ' + JSON.stringify(rr.input)).to.equal(true);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/embeddings",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "embeddings"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"github-copilot/text-embedding-3-small\",\n  \"input\": \"harness copilot embedding\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
